+`PendingUdpVerdicts` owns a joined pump that batches up to 1,024 terminal requests, locks backend write → correlator cell, and releases the backend lock before endpoint kernel handoff. Synchronous backend work uses `block_in_place` on multi-thread runtimes and runs inline on current-thread runtimes. The pump retains direct/block leases across caller cancellation; it rechecks original deadlines at dequeue, after backend locking, after grace and before each item, expiring late requests without conn mutation. A Direct request is late, and expires unarmed, once its deadline leaves less than its activation needs, which comes after that of the Direct flows armed before it in the batch: a 300 ms margin plus the activation work of those flows and its own, at a moving average per flow of the work without the waits for the backend, and never more than half the hold, so that a flow fresh from the queue is always armed and the average stays current. The batch's armed flows then accept their held originals off the backend lock, oldest first, and one backend acquisition activates every flow whose originals are out; a flow whose originals arrived meanwhile goes round again. Cancellation waits for armed Direct completion under that same deadline.
 
 A watchdog checks held cells independently and enforces the hard hold bound. Stale token, endpoint-generation, or backend-state mismatches drop without mutating a newer incarnation. A verdict failure or any failure after Direct has armed is process-fatal because userspace can no longer safely infer which originals the kernel accepted.
 
